title: Linux Update Tracker: Failed package transactions
agents: linux
catalog: os/misc
license: GPLv2
distribution: https://github.com/KeksDipp/checkmk-plugins
description:
 Shows failed and aborted package transactions of the last 30 days from the
 package manager history (APT history.log, DNF/YUM history), default {WARN}.
 A failure is ignored when all its packages were handled by a later successful
 transaction or none of them has a pending update anymore. A transaction still
 in progress is not counted.

 Also shows broken packages (half-installed or half-configured packages,
 problems reported by {dnf check}), default {WARN}.

discovery:
 One service is created if the package manager history or the broken package
 check is supported (APT, DNF, YUM - not Zypper).
